        "U2.59"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "TSC_G2_IO4"
      ],
      "observed": "C14 is connected from net TSC_G2_IO4 to itself: both C14 pins are listed on net TSC_G2_IO4, and that same net also contains the ground pins (J1.5, U2 VSS/VSSA, U3 VSS, U4 VSS, BOOT0, etc.). U2 pin 59 (PB7) is therefore also on the ground net. The SPICE deck models C14 as 0 to 0.",
      "expected": "The TSC sampling capacitor C14 should connect the PB7/TSC_G2_IO4 net to a separate GND net. PB7 should not be shorted directly to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"TSC_G2_IO4\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C14\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C14\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"59\") (pinfunction \"PB7\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C14 0 0 22n"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "`TSC_G2_IO4`: U2 pin 59 (`PB7`) — C14 (22 nF to GND) — this is the TSC sampling capacitor for the group"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The capacitive-touch sampling capacitor is shorted and PB7 is held at ground, disabling the TSC touch button and loading the MCU pin.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design otherwise matches the described NFC, display, SWD, and power topology, but the TSC sampling capacitor C14 is shorted: both its pins and MCU PB7 sit on the ground net, making the capacitive touch input nonfunctional."
}

